Complete the Linux lab
Step 1. Connect to the application server
Open your terminal (VS Code terminal or Kali terminal).
ssh user@app-server-ip


Replace the username and server IP with the credentials provided by KodeKloud.
Step 2. Create a service account
sudo useradd -m -s /usr/sbin/nologin service-user


What each option means:
Option	Purpose
useradd	Creates a new user
-m	Creates home directory
-s	Specifies login shell
/usr/sbin/nologin	Blocks interactive login

Step 3. Verify user creation
getent passwd service-user


Expected output format:
service-user:x:1003:1003::/home/service-user:/usr/sbin/nologin


UID and GID may differ on your server.
Step 4. Verify the home directory
ls -ld /home/service-user


Step 5. Check user identity
id service-user


This displays the UID, primary group and supplementary groups.
Step 6. Test non-interactive shell
sudo su service-user


Expected output:
This account is currently not available.


Expected result
 The account exists, but interactive shell access is denied.
Step 7. Additional verification
grep nologin /etc/passwd


This lists accounts configured with a nologin shell.

Important: A non-interactive shell prevents normal shell login; it does not prevent every possible form of access or stop authorized services from running under that identity.
